      {
        "text": "# async / await\n\n**`async`** is a keyword that tells a function to handle asynchronous operations, like requesting a list of book titles.\n\n**`await`** is a keyword used inside an async function that tells the program to wait for a Promise to resolve before moving to the next line.\n\n```\nconst fetchBooks = async () => {\n    const response = await fetch('/books');\n    return await response.json();\n};\n```",
